    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d95">

                <pb facs="0095" n="89" sameAs="frus:frus1942v02/pg89"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.60D/107: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Finland</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Schoenfeld</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Helsinki</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-10-21T11:00:00+02:00">October 21,
                            1942—11 a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 12:31 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>999. We learn that Foreign Minister Witting in next [<hi rendition="#italic">last
                        meeting of?</hi>] Foreign Affairs Committee reprimanded Salmiala<anchor
                        n="41" xml:id="d95-f1"/> of quasifascistic party when latter advocated break
                    with us saying Finland does not know how long war will last and that as small
                    country Finland must be careful not to lose contact with powerful nation which
                    is of great importance to her interests.</p>
                <p>It seems Witting is becoming more conscious that his own course has been too
                    pro-German and that he has been warned by group of men including Erkko of need
                    of following more closely President Ryti’s personal policy which goes about as
                    far as is considered safe.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Schoenfeld</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d95-f1" n="41" xml:id="d95-f1-content">
                <p>Prof. B. A. Salmiala, a leader of the Patriotic National Movement.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
